  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe STULONG study is a 20-year longitudinal research initiative focused on middle-aged men. The primary aim is to identify the prevalence of atherosclerosis risk factors (RFs) in a demographic considered highly susceptible to the condition. \n\nObjectives\n\nThe project aims to provide comprehensive data on the progression of atherosclerosis in middle-aged men, enabling the identification of key risk factors and prevalence trends over the duration of the study. This data will support preventive measures within this high-risk population.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Researchers: Conduct analyses and derive insights from the collected data.\n- Healthcare Providers: Utilize findings to improve preventive strategies.\n- Participants: Contribute data and benefit from potential health interventions.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Collection:\n   - Gather information on medical history, lifestyle, and health metrics over a 20-year period.\n   - Key data points include cholesterol levels, blood pressure, body mass index, smoking habits, and alcohol consumption.\n\n2. Data Analysis:\n   - Analyze the dataset to identify prevalence and trends in atherosclerosis risk factors.\n   - Cross-reference participant medical history with lifestyle changes and health outcomes.\n\n3. Reporting:\n   - Provide detailed reports on findings to stakeholders.\n   - Support preventive healthcare strategies with insights derived from the data.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Security: Ensure the protection of participant information with robust privacy measures.\n- Data Integration: Support seamless data aggregation from multiple sources for comprehensive analysis.\n- System Scalability: Handle extensive datasets as the study progresses over 20 years.\n- User Accessibility: Ensure accessible and clear presentation of data findings to various stakeholders.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0091\nCREATE TABLE `participants` (\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `study_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `sex` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enrollment_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participant_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `study_code` (`study_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medical_history` (\n  `history_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `condition_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `diagnosis_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`history_id`),\n  KEY `participant_id` (`participant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `medical_history_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`participant_id`) REFERENCES `participants` (`participant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `lifestyle_factors` (\n  `lifestyle_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `record_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `smoking_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `alcohol_consumption` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `physical_activity_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`lifestyle_id`),\n  KEY `participant_id` (`participant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `lifestyle_factors_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`participant_id`) REFERENCES `participants` (`participant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `health_metrics` (\n  `metric_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `measurement_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `cholesterol_total` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `cholesterol_hdl` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `cholesterol_ldl` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `systolic_blood_pressure` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `diastolic_blood_pressure` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body_mass_index` decimal(4,1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`metric_id`),\n  KEY `participant_id` (`participant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `health_metrics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`participant_id`) REFERENCES `participants` (`participant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `atherosclerosis_outcomes` (\n  `outcome_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `participant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assessment_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `atherosclerosis_present` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `severity_grade` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comments` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`outcome_id`),\n  KEY `participant_id` (`participant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `atherosclerosis_outcomes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`participant_id`) REFERENCES `participants` (`participant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
